      voice: 'gemini:Aoede | a relaxed, good-humoured co-host with a dry, understated wit; never exaggerated; speaks at a slightly brisk pace #ctx:1mrd9fb'
    '|a||Ninety-nine percent of a million: nine hundred and ninety thousand dollars.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4600
      voice: gemini:Sadaltager | a calm, warm mathematician who enjoys the puzzle; speaks at a slightly brisk, lively pace, never rushed
    '|a||Both boxes: a million and a thousand once in a hundred, a thousand the other ninety-nine times. That''s eleven thousand.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7520
      voice: 'gemini:Sadaltager | a calm, warm mathematician who enjoys the puzzle; speaks at a slightly brisk, lively pace, never rushed #ctx:iznhfg'
    '|b||Nine hundred and ninety thousand against eleven thousand. Take one box, and it isn''t close.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5400
      voice: 'gemini:Aoede | a relaxed, good-humoured co-host with a dry, understated wit; never exaggerated; speaks at a slightly brisk pace #ctx:pfraao'
    '|a||That''s the other trusted rule, expected value, from the St Petersburg lecture: weigh each outcome by how likely it is.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7880
      voice: 'gemini:Sadaltager | a calm, warm mathematician who enjoys the puzzle; speaks at a slightly brisk, lively pace, never rushed #ctx:1ils75l'
    '|a||And the Predictor needn''t be that good. How accurate must it be before one box comes out ahead?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6120
      voice: 'gemini:Sadaltager | a calm, warm mathematician who enjoys the puzzle; speaks at a slightly brisk, lively pace, never rushed #ctx:xe6owk'
    '|b||Click where one box starts to win.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2480
      voice: 'gemini:Aoede | a relaxed, good-humoured co-host with a dry, understated wit; never exaggerated; speaks at a slightly brisk pace #ctx:xy6rsm'
    '|a||Just over fifty percent. A Predictor barely better than a coin toss already makes one box the better bet.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6800
      voice: gemini:Sadaltager | a calm, warm mathematician who enjoys the puzzle; speaks at a slightly brisk, lively pace, never rushed
    '|b||So one table, read two ways, says take both and says take one.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5000
      voice: 'gemini:Aoede | a relaxed, good-humoured co-host with a dry, understated wit; never exaggerated; speaks at a slightly brisk pace #ctx:19t4jab'
    '|a||Each step looked innocent, and the conclusions clash, so one step must be wrong. The two camps disagree about which.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7640
      voice: 'gemini:Sadaltager | a calm, warm mathematician who enjoys the puzzle; speaks at a slightly brisk, lively pace, never rushed #ctx:gtohn8'
    '|a||Two-boxers see a choice as a lever. Your choice can''t put money in a box that''s already filled; it only tells you what''s probably inside.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8680
      voice: 'gemini:Sadaltager | a calm, warm mathematician who enjoys the puzzle; speaks at a slightly brisk, lively pace, never rushed #ctx:1mmpyow'
    '|a||One-boxers see it as a clue. The dominance table assumes the box doesn''t depend on you; with this Predictor, what you choose and what''s inside go together.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9000
      voice: 'gemini:Sadaltager | a calm, warm mathematician who enjoys the puzzle; speaks at a slightly brisk, lively pace, never rushed #ctx:1jjprx4'
    '|b||And the one-boxers walk off with the money. That must sting.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3880
      voice: 'gemini:Aoede | a relaxed, good-humoured co-host with a dry, understated wit; never exaggerated; speaks at a slightly brisk pace #ctx:2urnfe'
    '|a||It does. In 1981 David Lewis, a two-boxer, titled a paper after their taunt: Why ain''cha rich?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8240
      voice: 'gemini:Sadaltager | a calm, warm mathematician who enjoys the puzzle; speaks at a slightly brisk, lively pace, never rushed #ctx:6rgvry'
    '|a||His answer: the Predictor rewards people who take one box. For a two-boxer, the million was never on offer.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7160
      voice: 'gemini:Sadaltager | a calm, warm mathematician who enjoys the puzzle; speaks at a slightly brisk, lively pace, never rushed #ctx:1rmuftb'
    '|a||Philosophers call these causal and evidential decision theory.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4120
      voice: 'gemini:Sadaltager | a calm, warm mathematician who enjoys the puzzle; speaks at a slightly brisk, lively pace, never rushed #ctx:ydeyv4'
    '|b||Have they settled it?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 1440
      voice: 'gemini:Aoede | a relaxed, good-humoured co-host with a dry, understated wit; never exaggerated; speaks at a slightly brisk pace #ctx:1ypnjtp'
    '|a||Not even close. In a 2020 survey of philosophers, 31 percent took one box and 39 percent both; the rest wouldn''t commit.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9480
      voice: 'gemini:Sadaltager | a calm, warm mathematician who enjoys the puzzle; speaks at a slightly brisk, lively pace, never rushed #ctx:sgv5q9'
    '|b||Now the specialists, the decision theorists. What share of them take both boxes? Click the line.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6640
      voice: 'gemini:Aoede | a relaxed, good-humoured co-host with a dry, understated wit; never exaggerated; speaks at a slightly brisk pace #ctx:1was21d'
    '|a||Seventy-three percent: the specialists lean hard towards both. Outside philosophy, polls come out much closer to even.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7880
      voice: gemini:Sadaltager | a calm, warm mathematician who enjoys the puzzle; speaks at a slightly brisk, lively pace, never rushed
    '|a||And ordinary people act on clues too. In 1984, Quattrone and Tversky had students hold an arm in ice-cold water, exercise, and try again. Some were told a healthy heart shows as more tolerance for cold; others, less.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 16400
      voice: 'gemini:Sadaltager | a calm, warm mathematician who enjoys the puzzle; speaks at a slightly brisk, lively pace, never rushed #ctx:1psmztx'
    '|a||On the second try, each group''s tolerance moved towards the sign of a long life. They acted for the good sign, as a one-boxer does.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9480
      voice: 'gemini:Sadaltager | a calm, warm mathematician who enjoys the puzzle; speaks at a slightly brisk, lively pace, never rushed #ctx:17qiu5x'
    '|b||Changing the sign without touching the heart.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2600
      voice: 'gemini:Aoede | a relaxed, good-humoured co-host with a dry, understated wit; never exaggerated; speaks at a slightly brisk pace #ctx:1hidgkh'
    '|a||So the split is about what a choice is: a lever on the world, or a clue about it. Usually the two agree; Newcomb''s Predictor pulls them apart.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10200
      voice: 'gemini:Sadaltager | a calm, warm mathematician who enjoys the puzzle; speaks at a slightly brisk, lively pace, never rushed #ctx:gfigc3'
    '|b||Flossers live longer, so tonight you floss, though you know flossing does nothing for your health. Which box-taker reasons like you?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8520
      voice: 'gemini:Aoede | a relaxed, good-humoured co-host with a dry, understated wit; never exaggerated; speaks at a slightly brisk pace #ctx:1wt9fju'
    '|b||A one-boxer: you''re choosing for the good sign, not for what the choice causes.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5880
      voice: gemini:Aoede | a relaxed, good-humoured co-host with a dry, understated wit; never exaggerated; speaks at a slightly brisk pace
    '|b||So, one box or two? Whichever you tapped at the start, about half the room thinks you''ve missed something obvious.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7000
      voice: gemini:Aoede | a relaxed, good-humoured co-host with a dry, understated wit; never exaggerated; speaks at a slightly brisk pace
    '|a||Next: Can any voting rule be fair? Arrow''s impossibility theorem':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5840
      voice: gemini:Sadaltager | a calm, warm mathematician who enjoys the puzzle; speaks at a slightly brisk, lively pace, never rushed
    '|b||The Predictor saw that coming.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2040
      voice: gemini:Aoede | a relaxed, good-humoured co-host with a dry, understated wit; never exaggerated; speaks at a slightly brisk pace
    '|b||A respectable haul from both boxes.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2760
      voice: gemini:Aoede | a relaxed, good-humoured co-host with a dry, understated wit; never exaggerated; speaks at a slightly brisk pace
    '|b||The Predictor kept the million this time.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2120
      voice: gemini:Aoede | a relaxed, good-humoured co-host with a dry, understated wit; never exaggerated; speaks at a slightly brisk pace
    '|b||Fair enough: you took neither box.':
